<p>This page helps property owners determine if SR-177 affects their property and provides step-by-step guidance on what to do at each phase of the project.</p>

<hr class="divider">

<div class="section-label">Step 1: Determine If Your Property Is Affected</div>
<h2>Geographic Screening</h2>

<p><strong>The SR-177 corridor will primarily affect properties based on proximity to the planned alignment.</strong> As of April 2026, UDOT is studying an alignment along 5100 West. The impact zones are:</p>

<ul style="margin: 20px 0 20px 24px; line-height: 2.2;">
  <li><strong>Acquisition Zone (250 feet):</strong> Properties within the right-of-way are subject to acquisition once the project is funded. Standard right-of-way is 250 feet wide (125 feet on each side of the centerline).</li>
  <li><strong>Noise Evaluation Zone (500 feet):</strong> Properties within ~500 feet of the highway centerline are evaluated for noise impacts (66 dBA threshold). Some may qualify for sound wall mitigation.</li>
  <li><strong>Construction Impact Zone:</strong> Properties near the corridor may experience temporary construction traffic, dust, vibration, and noise during the construction phase.</li>
  <li><strong>Indirect Impact Zone:</strong> Properties along feeder roads and at the 4000 South interchange may experience increased traffic after construction.</li>
</ul>

<div class="callout">
  <p><strong>To find your property's location:</strong></p>
  <ol>
    <li>Visit <a href="https://www.webercountyutah.gov/assessor/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Weber County Assessor's Office (webercountyutah.gov/assessor)</a></li>
    <li>Search for your address or parcel number in their online mapping tool</li>
    <li>Note the parcel number (format: TR-##-[##]-[###]-###)</li>
    <li>Register for State Environmental Study updates at <a href="https://udotinput.utah.gov/sr177extension" rel="noopener noreferrer">udotinput.utah.gov/sr177extension</a> to receive alignment maps when published</li>
  </ol>
</div>

