<div class="section-label">Step 2: Understand Your Options</div>
<h2>Decision Tree: What Should You Do?</h2>

<div class="decision-tree">
  <p><strong>If your property is in Phase 3 (1800 N to 4000 S, near 5100 W):</strong></p>

  <div style="margin: 20px 0; padding: 15px; background: #f5f5f5; border-left: 4px solid #0066cc;">
    <p><strong>Option A: Wait for Formal Alignment (Recommended for most owners)</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Register for State Environmental Study updates at udotinput.utah.gov/sr177extension</li>
      <li>Wait for Draft State Environmental Study (Fall 2026) to see formal alignment maps</li>
      <li>Determine if your property is actually in the right-of-way or noise zone</li>
      <li>Make decisions after you have certainty</li>
      <li><strong>Pros:</strong> Maximum information; time to prepare; can negotiate from informed position</li>
      <li><strong>Cons:</strong> Longer uncertainty; property value may decline as project becomes real</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div style="margin: 20px 0; padding: 15px; background: #f5f5f5; border-left: 4px solid #0066cc;">
    <p><strong>Option B: Sell Now to UDOT Corridor Preservation Program</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>If UDOT approaches you, you can choose to negotiate and sell voluntarily</li>
      <li>You receive fair market value appraisal + relocation assistance</li>
      <li>Sale is final; you exit the situation entirely</li>
      <li><strong>Pros:</strong> Certainty; get compensation before alignment finalized; clear the uncertainty</li>
      <li><strong>Cons:</strong> May receive below-market price; miss potential appreciation if project delayed; lose family land</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div style="margin: 20px 0; padding: 15px; background: #f5f5f5; border-left: 4px solid #0066cc;">
    <p><strong>Option C: Document & Prepare (Proactive approach)</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Commission a professional property appraisal now (while funding is uncertain)</li>
      <li>Document current property condition (photos, video, surveys)</li>
      <li>Get a title search and mortgage payoff estimate</li>
      <li>Contact elected representatives and UDOT with concerns</li>
      <li>Participate in public State Environmental Study comment periods</li>
      <li><strong>Pros:</strong> Better positioned for negotiation; stronger documentation if compensation is disputed later</li>
      <li><strong>Cons:</strong> Costs money; may highlight property to UDOT; doesn't resolve uncertainty</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

